description:
The, Town Council, as the local planning agency, in accordance with the Local Government Comprehensive Planning Act of 1975, F.S. §§ 163.3161—3211, shall: (1) Conduct the comprehensive planning program and prepare the comprehensive plan or elements or portions thereof for the town;
(2) Coordinate said comprehensive plan or elements or portions thereof with the comprehensive plans of other appropriate local governments of the state;
(3) Recommend said comprehensive plan or elements or portions thereof to the town council for adoption; and
(4) Monitor and oversee the effectiveness and status of the comprehensive plan and recommend to the town council such changes in the comprehensive plan as may be required from time to time.
